  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"Isotropic 3D electron microscopy data of isolated murine pancreatic islets treated with low glucose\" has garnered 12 citations, indicating measurable academic uptake. Furthermore, it has been reused in at least 13 downstream analyses, demonstrating its significance in related research domains.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Released in 2022, this dataset has a notable impact within the fields of endocrinology and cell biology, allowing researchers to explore the ultrastructure of pancreatic islets under specific conditions. The high visibility of this work is reflected in its recognition by leading platforms, as indicated by its citations in reputable publications like Nature Communications and its presence on preprint servers like bioRxiv, where it has gained additional interest.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The provided dataset is an essential resource for studies concerning islet biology and related metabolic diseases. Its collection methodology and detailed insights into the pancreatic islet structure enable researchers to advance their understanding of insulin secretion and cellular interactions in diabetes.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite the absence of downloads and online mentions, the academic community has shown engagement through citations, indicating ongoing interest in the findings. Notably, an associated preprint has received 10 citations, illustrating the dataset's relevance in ongoing scientific discourse.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, this dataset represents a valuable contribution to the scientific literature, fostering further exploration into the dynamics of pancreatic islets and their role in metabolic regulation. Its reuse across various studies underscores its lasting importance in the field.</p>",
